1. What Is Inheritance?

Inheritance is one of the four main pillars of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP).

Definition: Inheritance is a mechanism in Java in which one class acquires accessible fields and methods from another class.

Inheritance helps us reuse existing code and reduce duplication.

Example

Consider an animal application.

Animal is the parent class.

Dog is the child class.

A dog can use inherited methods from the Animal class.

A dog can also define its own methods.
